G3705.def:
ὅραμα, -τος, τό
(ὁράω), [in LXX for חָזוֹן, מַרְאֶה, etc. ;] 
that which is seen; 
__(a) a sight, spectacle: Matthieu 17:9, Actes 7:31; 
__(b) an appearance, vision: Actes 9:10, 12 (Rec.) Actes 10:3, 17 10:19 11:5 12:9 16:9-10 18:9 (cf. ὀπτασία).†

G3709.def:
ὀργή, -ῆς, ἡ 
[in LXX chiefly for אַף, also for חָרוֹן, חֵמָה, קָצַף, etc. ;] 
__1 1, impulse, propensity, disposition. 
__2. anger, wrath; 
__(a) of men: Marc 3:5, Éphésiens 4:31, Colossiens 3:8, 1 Timothée 2:8, Jacques 1:19-20; 
__(b) of God; 
__α that reaction of the divine nature against sin which in anthropomorphic language is called anger: Romains 1:18 9:22 12:19, (ICC, in l), 1 Thessaloniciens 1:10 2:16, Hébreux 3:11 4:3" (LXX) Apocalypse 14:10 16:19 19:15; 
__β of the effect of God's anger: Matthieu 3:7, Luc 3:7 21:23, Jean 3:36, Romains 2:5, 8 3:5 4:15 5:9 13:4-5 Éphésiens 5:6, Colossiens 3:6, 1 Thessaloniciens 5:9, Jacques 1:20, Apocalypse 6:16-17 11:18; σκεύη ὀργῆς, Romains 9:22; τέκνα ὀργῆς, Éphésiens 2:3.†
SYN.: see: θυμός

G3717.def:
ὀρθός, -ή, -όν 
[in LXX chiefly for יָשָׁר ;] 
straight; 
__(a) in height, straight, upright: Actes 14:10; 
__(b) in line, straight, direct: figuratively, Hébreux 12:13 (LXX).†

G3745.def:
ὅσος, -η, -ον, 
correlat. of τοσοῦτος, 
how much, how many, how great, how far, how long, as much as, etc. (= Lat. quantus); 
__(a) of number and quantity: m. pl., Matthieu 14:36, Marc 3:10, Romains 2:12, al.; n. pl., Matthieu 17:12, Marc 10:21, Luc 11:8, al.; πάτνες (πάντα) ὅ., Matthieu 13:46, Luc 4:40, al.; before οὗτοι (ταῦτα), Romains 8:14, Philippiens 4:8; with indic., Marc 6:56, Apocalypse 3:19; with subjc. Marc 3:28, al.; ὅ. ἄν, Matthieu 18:18, Jean 11:22, al.; 
__(b) of measure and degree: Marc 3:8, Luc 8:39, Actes 9:13; in compar. sent., ὅσον before μᾶλλον, Marc 7:36; καθ᾽ ὅσον, with compar.. Hébreux 3:3; before τοσοῦτο, Hébreux 7:20; οὕτως, Hébreux 9:27; τοσαύτῳ, with compar. before ὅσῳ, with compar., Hébreux 1:4; ἐφ᾽ ὅσον, inasmuch as, Matthieu 25:40, 45 Romains 11:13; 
__(with) of space and time: Apocalypse 21:16; ἐφ᾽ ὅσον, as long as, Matthieu 9:15, 2 Pierre 1:13; ἐφ᾽ ὅ. χρόνον, Romains 7:1, 1 Corinthiens 7:39, Galates 4:1; ἔτι μικρὸν ὅσον ὅσον, yet how very short a time, Hébreux 10:37 (LXX).

G3748.def:
ὅστις, ἥτις, ὅ τι (also written ὅ, τι and ὅτι; see LS, see word; WH, §411; Tdf., Pr., 111), in NT scarcely ever except in nom. (M, Pr., 91), the only instance of the oblique cases being found in ἕως ὅτου (see: ἕως), relative of indef. reference (related to simple ὅς as Lat. quisquis to qui), 
whoever, anyone who; 
__(a) of an indef. person or thing: in general statements, Matthieu 5:39, 41 13:12, and freq., Luc 14:27, Galates 5:4, al.; in relative sentences, Matthieu 7:26, Luc 15:7, Philippiens 3:7, al.; πᾶς, with indic., Matthieu 7:24 10:32; ὅ ἄν (ἐάν), with subjc., Matthieu 12:50 13:12, Jean 14:13, 1 Corinthiens 16:2, Galates 5:10, al.; 
__(b) of a definite person or thing, indicating quality, "either generic, which, as other like things, or essential, which by its very nature" (Hort on 1 Pierre 2:11), who is such as: Matthieu 2:6 7:26, Luc 2:10 7:37, Jean 8:53, Actes 7:53, Romains 6:2, 1 Corinthiens 3:17, Galates 4:24, Éphésiens 1:23, al.; 
__(with) where the relative sentence expresses a reason, consequence, etc. (M, Pr., 92), seeing that he (it, they), and he (it, they): Luc 8:3 10:42, Actes 10:47 11:28, Philippiens 4:3, al.; 
__(d) as in Ionic and late Greek (Bl., §50, 1; M, Pr., l.with), differing but little from ὅς: Luc 2:4 9:30, Actes 17:10, Apocalypse 12:13.

G3752.def:
ὅταν (for ὅτ᾽ ἄν = ὅτε ἄν), 
temporal particle, 
with a conditional sense, usually of things expected to occur in an indefinite future; 
__1. prop., whenever; 
__(a) (a) with subjc. praes.: Matthieu 6:2, 5 Marc 14:7, Luc 11:36, Jean 7:27, Actes 23:35, 1 Corinthiens 3:4, al.; ἕως τ. ἡμέρας ἐκείνης, ὅ., Matthieu 26:29, Marc 14:25; before τότε, 1 Thessaloniciens 5:3; 
__(b) with subjc. aor. (M, Pr., 185): Matthieu 5:11, Marc 4:15, Luc 6:22, Jean 2:10 8:28 (Field, Notes, 94), 10:4, al. 
__2. As in Hom. (LS, see word), but not in cl. prose, with indic., when (M, Pr., 167f.; Bl., §65, 9): with impf., Marc 3:11(cf. Genèse 38:9, al.); with praes., Marc 11:25; with fut.. Apocalypse 4:9 (Swete, in l.); with aor., Marc 11:19, Apocalypse 8:1 (Swete, in ll.; M, Pr., 168, 248; Field, Notes, 35).

G3757.def:
oὗ
(prop. genitive of ὅς), 
adv. of place, where, whither; 
__(a) in answer to the question "where?" (= ubi): Matthieu 2:9 18:20, Luc 4:16-17 23:53, Actes 1:13 2:2 7:29 12:12 16:13 20:6, 8 25:10 28:14, Romains 9:26" (LXX), Colossiens 3:1, Hébreux 3:9" (LXX), Apocalypse 17:15; of condition, Romains 4:15 5:20, 2 Corinthiens 3:17; 
__(b) in answer to the question "whither?" (= quo): Matthieu 28:16, Luc 10:1 24:28; before ἐάν, with subjc., 1 Corinthiens 16:6.†

G3778.def:
οὗτος, αὕτη, τοῦτο, genitive, τούτου, ταύτης, τούτου, 
[in LXX chiefly for זֹאת ,זֶה ;] 
demonstr. pron. (related to ἐκεῖνος as hic to ille), 
this; 
__1. as subst., this one, he; 
__(a) absol.: Matthieu 3:17, Marc 9:7, Luc 7:44, 45, Jean 1:15, Actes 2:15, al.; expressing contempt (cl.), Matthieu 13:55, 56, Marc 6:2, 3, Jean 6:42, al.; εἰς τοῦτο, Marc 1:38, Romains 14:9; μετὰ τοῦτο (ταῦτα; V. Westc. on Jean 5:1), Jean 2:12 11:7, al.; 
__(b) epanaleptic (referring to what precedes): Matthieu 5:19, Marc 3:35, Luc 9:48, Jean 6:46, Romains 7:10, al.; 
__(with) proleptic (referring to what follows): before ἵνα (Bl., §69, 6), Luc 1:43, Jean 3:19 (and freq.) 15:8, Romains 14:9, al.; before ὅτι, Luc 10:11, Jean 9:3o, Actes 24:14, Romains 2:3, al.; ὅπως, Romains 9:17; ἐάν, Jean 13:35; 
__(d) special idioms: τοῦτο μὲν . . . τ. δέ (cl), partly . . . partly. Hébreux 10:33; καὶ τοῦτο (τοῦτον, ταῦτα), and that (him) too, Romains 13:11, 1 Corinthiens 2:2, Hébreux 11:12; τοῦτ᾽ ἐστιν, Matthieu 27:46.
__2. As adj., with subst.; 
__(a) with art. 
__(α) before the art.: Matthieu 12:32, Marc 9:29, Luc 7:44, Jean 4:15, Romains 11:24, Apocalypse 19:9, al.; 
__(β) after the noun: Matthieu 3:9, Marc 12:16, Luc 11:31, Jean 4:13, Actes 6:13, Romains 15:28, 1 Corinthiens 1:20, Apocalypse 2:24, al.; 
__(b) with subst. anarth. (with predicative force; Bl., §49, 4): Luc 1:36 2:2 24:21, Jean 2:11 4:54 21:14, 2 Corinthiens 13:1.

G3780.def:
οὐχί 
strengthened form of οὐ, 
not; 
__(a) in neg. sentences, not, not at all: Luc 1:60 12:51, Jean 13:10, al.; 
__(b) more frequently in questions where an affirm. ans. is expected (Lat. nonne) : Matthieu 5:46-47, Luc 6:39, Jean 11:9, al.

G3788.def:
ὀφθαλμός, -οῦ, ὁ, 
[in LXX chiefly for עַיִן ;] 
the eye (as in cl., chiefly pl.): Matthieu 5:38, Marc 9:47, Luc 6:41, Jean 9:6, al.; τοὺς ὀ. ἐξορύθσσειν (figuratively), Galates 4:15; ἐπᾶραι, Luc 6:20, Jean 6:5; ἀνοῖξα, Actes 9:40; id., of restoring sight, Matthieu 20:33, Jean 9:10, al.; ἐν ῥιπῇ ὀφθαλμοῦ, 1 Corinthiens 15:52; by anthropom., of God, Hébreux 4:13, 1 Pierre 3:12; pleonastically (cf. Thackeray, Gr., 42f.), εἶδον οἱ ὀ. μοθ, Luc 2:30 (similarly, ib. 4:20 10:23, Jean 12:40, 1 Corinthiens 2:9, 1 Jean 1:1, Apocalypse 1:7). Metaphorical (as otherwise in cl.; see LS, see word); 
__(a) of ethical qualities: ὀ. πονηρός (meton., for envy; cf. Heb. עַיִן רַע, Proverbes 28:22; cf. Sir.14:10 34:13), Matthieu 6:22, 23 Marc 7:22, Luc 11:34; ἁπλοῦς, Matthieu 6:22, Luc 11:34; ἐπιθυμία (which see) ὀφθαλμῶν (cf. Ecclésiaste 4:8, Sir.14:9), 1 Jean 2:16; ὀ. μεστοὶ μοιχαλἰδος, 2 Pierre 2:14; 
__(b) of mental vision: Matthieu 13:15, Marc 8:18, Luc 19:42, Jean 12:40, Romains 11:8, Galates 3:1, Éphésiens 1:18, al.; ἐν ὀφθαλμοῖς before genitive (on the absence of the art., seeBl, §46, 9.II; M, Pr., 81), Matthieu 21:42, Marc 12:11.
